Z||000003||stimpy||01-29-2001||11:27 PM||||I had the good fortune of attending highschool in Waterloo, Belgium. Saw many many trick rare rides.  I remember a Lancia Stratos (lime green with the wicked Dino V6) Lambo Urraco, Iso Grifo, Shelby GT500 convertable, my dad's Pantera, got passed by a Boxer 512 doing at least 160 driving back from Spain...<BR>Memories(sigh) ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Will||01-29-2001||11:52 PM||||Not so much the cars I've seen, but <I>where</I> I've seen them.<P>Just last week I saw a targa Viper here in Blacksburg.<BR>Last summer I saw a 355 Ferrari drive through the thriving metropolis of Shenandoah, VA.<P>I've seen a Ferrari 308 and Testarossa on the interstate. I saw a Testarossa up on a trailer on the interstate on another occasion.<BR> My parents saw a Ferrari 550 a few months ago.<BR> There's at least one Hummer in Blacksburg, too, along with a couple of NSX's.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||01-30-2001||02:23 AM||||a testa rossa and a few skylines in oman my last guard trip.||||reg||1
Z||000006||onfire||01-30-2001||04:06 AM||||I seen a Ferrari F40 (not a kit) about a year ago, on hiway 18.<P>I also seen a F355 convertable downtown Seattle. <P>And a white GT R Viper<P>There's actually alot of Vipers and Hummers around here. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||01-30-2001||07:54 AM||||ferrari's shmarrari's... there all over town!  a local, bought the first F-40, and used to drive it to work!  he put like 10,000 miles on that thing in 2 or 3 years!<P>i used to work on Bently Turbo-R's (a 2 ton vehicle that went 0-60 in under 6 seconds!), among others... we installed car phones in high dollar automobiles.<P>but probably the neatest thing that i have seen; was last year, i went home for lunch, when i passed a blue viper coupe (with white stripe) going in the opisite direction on a country road, and on the way back... in the exact same spot (but other side of the road), i passed a shelby cobra, with identical paint scheme!<P>that was wierd!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||01-30-2001||07:58 AM||||I saw one of the original Batmobiles driving down East Main st in Columbus a couple years ago. Have also seen a 1954 Mercedes 300SL roadster and a 55 SLR.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 01-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT Bastard||01-30-2001||08:08 AM||||Around town I've seen an Acura NSX, A yellow Lotus Espirit, a few Vipers, and Ferrari(prolly a kit.)||||reg||1
Z||000010||Tigger||01-30-2001||08:57 AM||||I've seen a number of Vipers, prob most significant one was a hardtop version with the blue and white stripes Indy 500 pace car edition.<P>Last summer...<P>Followed a yellow Prowler with manufacture plates. (not extremely rare, but don't see everyday)<P>Delorean.<P>Red Diablo pulled up to a light across the intersection from me.  Made a right turn and was goooone.  Real thing, V12 sounds and all.<BR>(If only he had pulled up to the light beside me, then he would've finally witnessed the true uleashed, unheard of, and unimaginable power that can come from a 2.5 that makes all supercars bow down to the Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> j/k)<P>Many others...<P>||||reg||6
Z||000011||GeeDee86GT||01-30-2001||10:52 AM||||Passed a guy last summer, he was driving a 50's Messerschmitt Kabinroller.  Man, he was grinnin' from ear to ear. Must have been fun.<BR>Gary||||reg||6
Z||000012||FieroLisa||01-30-2001||11:48 AM||||<BR>My friend's family has a new Hummer in the tiny little town of Suffield, OH, and they drove it around, and let us kids take it to prom and such, along with their 2 vettes. Saw a black ferrari (real not kit) there too. Um other stuff, I just don't remember. When my dad was a kid, he drove his Lancia to school every day (when it wasn't in the shop of course)<BR>Oh yah and one of my ex's grandfathers had a teal Edsel with a plaid teal top.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroLisa (edited 01-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||fiero56||01-30-2001||12:06 PM||||There are quite a few nice cars around here. Not a whole lot of rare ones for the area, compared to places like Michigan or something(no offense to Michgan dwellers, but I hate that state). In the summer there is a Vector that lives somewhere in the neighborhood, it usually went by several times a day. Lots of "uncommon" cars seem like daily sights in the summer: Diablo, Countach, Viper, NSX(too many of 'em here), any Ferrarri, etc. I remember 87ECO5 and I were on our way to the yard, and there were 3 Ferrarrris at one intersection, all heading different directions, not with a group or anything. My rich a$$ neighbors had a wedding at their place last summer for one of their kids, and the whole yard was full of exotics, was pretty cool. C5s at every corner, even in the salt and snow.||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||01-30-2001||12:07 PM||||a Koenig Quad Turbo Testarossa the owner of 4 or 5 chain stereo shops around here drives a Black one. #3 of 6 built. over 700hp to the ground!!! and of course a LAME useless wing... but hey it was expensive so he needed it. just cause you have money doesn't mean you have taste.  ||||reg||1
Z||000015||sqoach||01-30-2001||01:18 PM||||well, in my tiny town of 5000 people, there's not much to see. my car actually gets some attention. but the one i can remember the most that got attention was a yellow plymouth prowler. it was pretty sweet.<P>there's also been car shows and cruises here, and of course that draws attention.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000016||DaRkLoRD||01-30-2001||01:29 PM||||in my home town I've seen 2 hummers, there's 3 porsches, a few jags.. I've also seen a testarossa (not sure if it was a kit or not)<BR>and also a MINT cherry red 86 Fiero SE.. I've only seen that one 3 times. the owner keeps it in his garage most of the time.<P>in Toronto I've seen more porsches than I can count.. at least 1 viper, acura NSX, Ferrari 328, and tons of vettes.<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 01-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Standard||01-30-2001||01:51 PM||||See plenty of Porsches up here, but I also live not too far away from one of the biggest Porsche/Audi dealers around.  Trying to get a job there as a runner.. don't think I'd mind driving around Porsches all day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Seen a few hummers, 2 or 3 RT/10 Vipers, one GTS-R, a real Ferrari F355, Lambo Diablo (not sure if it was a kit or real), Lotus Espirit, and those super rare honda civics with monster wings  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||
