Z||000021||2M4 Dale||01-30-2001||06:22 PM||||There is a fellow who drives around in a Brubaker Box in Mansfield. There also was a 1978 (I think) Ferrari 308 for sale at a little used car lot here last summer. Several of the old cars seen in the film Shawshank Redemtion live just down the road from me (and the guy does drive them). About 30 minutes Northeast of me is a guy who customizes Hummers for the Saudi Royalty and we see those out from time to time. ||||reg||7
Z||000022||ray b||01-30-2001||07:22 PM|||| if pip will down load i got neat pic to post of my dads front yard to show.<BR> in 1973 walked out of super sub shop and in parking lot was a huge old car with a  horse shoe shaped rad. 23" alum. wheels ,yellow paint, 1/2 block long giant with every detail perfect best workmanship i have ever seen in any car ever and unchanged most valuable at least $1,000,000 in 1973 and today $25m up. most sought after car of all time.bugaitti ROYAL only 7 made and all sold to kings .at the sub shop!!!! ray||||reg||14
Z||000023||ray b||01-30-2001||10:53 PM||||postv <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3cars.gif"> <BR>first is alum. boby on 30s M G called gadabout done by my dad next is french 39 paris show car raced at le manz by delhase or dellara two diff co.not sure whicth dads bud's car.last is scarab but not 50 co. that raced but 30's diff co. made less than 10 had ford flat head v8 in rear chain drive to gear box under motor early mini van like car was dads driver in ww2 300000 miles fords v8 lasted 100000 each . ||||reg||1
Z||000024||2xsess||01-31-2001||08:18 AM||||Hummers..hah, I see them everyday. Of course they're not as pretty as the gray one I've seen running around town. <BR>I'll take a pick of a few of them today maybe.<P>In West PLam beach you'll see all kinds of exotics. Diablo convertables,Prowlers, Jags,Ferraris, Contauchs( real ones)Porsches out the butt, and of course NSXs rolling around all over the place. A few Calloway and Lingenfelter Vettes. I remember seeing a REd Viper GTS in a parking lot when they first came out, it was a plumber company,like Rotto-router or something.<P>I think Fieros were the rarest thing sited.<P>Here in Tiny little Hinesville GA the rarest thing I've seen is a bright red Prowler. And of course Vettes, even a C5 or 2, One Viper so far. There are some nice ones in Savannah though.<P>Hey Trav,Raydar, you should see lots of Panoz cars around there too, I saw on TV last night that they're made in Atlanta GA.<p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 01-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||p4n1c||01-31-2001||08:46 AM||||Porsche's out the wazzo here, Diablo(which I think was a kit), More Ferrari's than you can count(there was a dealership near my old place, 355s, F-50s, and some older ones that I can't identify), Stealth R/Ts out the wazzo, Couple Viper's, few Fiero's(   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) most of them beaters, but a few nice ones,  Corvette Stingrays to C5s, Jags, Prowlers and I think that's it.  Probably seen more, but can't remember.  Fiero is definitly the rarest around here.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 01-31-2001).]||||reg||1
