Z||000033||sluppy123||02-02-2001||05:36 PM||||I was entered in a car show with these cars. My 87' GT got third.<P>This Car got 2nd- 1999 Lotus Esprit V8<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=7653930&p=30139721&Sequence=0"> <P>This was first- 1967 Iso Griffo. I talked with the owner who said it Was built in Italy and powered by a chevy 350.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=7653930&p=30139312&Sequence=0"> <P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT-Leather, Lowered and On The Bottle<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=7653930&p=37756786&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||10
Z||000034||Alex2004||02-04-2001||11:52 AM||||Probably the rarest car i have seen was either a Red Ferrari Testerossa Convertible in Ft. Lauderdale ( i was 10 ) or a black Ferrari 355 at a  gas station in Stuart Florida x-mas of 99.  But when we went to a HUGE Jaguar Dealer in West Palm Beach, there was a new Aston Martin Vantage Convertible in there, so that was probably the rarest i have seen. <P>Alex...||||reg||10
Z||000035||Sleeper||02-04-2001||07:07 PM||||i live in a suburb of LA so i see a bunch of rich fools driving their high priced sportscars:<P>1 F-50 & 1 F-40 in newport beach<BR>dozens of ferrari 308's, 355's, testarossa's all over hollywood and beverly hills(1 355 riced out with stickers too)<BR>1 McLaren F1 in the San Fernando Valley(don't think their even allowed in Cali)<BR>every porsche in the book<BR>1 vega and 1 pinto(opps wrong list)<BR>sretched Hummers and Lincoln Navitgators(spelled wrong, i think)<BR>1 pantara down my street(with a 355 windsor)<BR>3 skylines in my city<BR>and i think i seen a 1940 Ferrari Barchetta down on sunset strip, just making a guess from a pic.<P>i've seen all these car but no lambo's(just in showrooms)<P><BR>my friends dad says he crusing with one of his friends back in 1985 down through Death Valley, and oh, they were driving an 84 935 slop nose porsche going 150+(just crusing). and all of a sudden a red car just blew past them going like 190 or so. he said it was just screaming past them. my friends dad said he never knew what kinda car that was...(i didn't know there was a car that could go that fast in the 80's)<P><BR>------------------<BR>85 GT<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels, Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering spring, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, Chris West's Strut Tower Bar, Accel Super Coil, Accel Wires, K&N filter and Optima Battery.<p>[This message has been edited by Sleeper (edited 02-04-2001).]||||reg||1
